1
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
(Blossom Through the Cloud)

2
00:01:35,001 --> 00:01:37,960
(Adapted from the novel on JJWXC, "Landing on My Heart", by Qiao Yao)

3
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:34,840
It's raining.

4
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,800
Is it raining?

5
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,200
Don't get caught in the rain.

6
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,480
Otherwise, I'll be worried.

7
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,920
(Episode 20: Mayday)

8
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:19,000
The exterior is the face of the hotel,

9
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:20,159
but to make it a hit,

10
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:21,280
you need a selling point.

11
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,039
So I plan to spend...

12
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,959
most of the renovation budget...

13
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,319
on two main areas, refurbishing the hotel's facade...

14
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,800
and renovating the Sunset Restaurant.

15
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:30,839
However, since my budget is limited,

16
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,040
the exterior walls will just get a fresh coat of paint.

17
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,799
As for the Sunset Restaurant, I'm planning to place it...

18
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,880
in the second-floor lobby and terrace.

19
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,480
By then, the outdoor viewing spots...

20
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:40,680
and the seats by the window...

21
00:03:40,681 --> 00:03:42,520
will become viral photo spots.

22
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,039
At that point, the number of seats...

23
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,080
becomes very important.

24
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,519
Demand should exceed supply...

25
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,880
to make people want to queue up,

26
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,959
but at the same time, it shouldn't be so overcrowded...

27
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:50,960
that it puts people off.

28
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:52,920
As for the food,

29
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,040
I'm thinking,

30
00:03:54,041 --> 00:03:56,280
besides the hotel's breakfast buffet,

31
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,800
we'll serve brunch at 11 am,

32
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,079
afternoon tea in the afternoon,

33
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,199
and turn it into a restaurant and bar at night.

34
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,480
We won't do complicated cooking.

35
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:05,680
But I have three requirements.

36
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,040
It must look good,

37
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,840
not taste bad, and look exceptionally good.

38
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:12,999
"Not taste bad"?

39
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,360
Isn't that a bit perfunctory?

40
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:17,160
I can't find a top-tier chef.

41
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,880
Looking good is my bottom line.

42
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,960
I'll help you find a chef. Go on.

43
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,480
For the banquet hall, I'm thinking...

44
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,079
of renting it out.

45
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,720
I'll rent it to people who do immersive LARP games.

46
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,480
Something like...

47
00:04:29,481 --> 00:04:31,319
a "Hotel Horror" entertainment project.

48
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,759
That way, I'll save on renovation costs...

49
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:33,856
and still collect a venue fee.

50
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,159
I can even lower the fee for them,

51
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,160
but on one condition.

52
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,960
It has to be a 2-day, 1-night event.

53
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,640
This way, they can increase their price per guest,

54
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,360
and I can sell my guest rooms.

55
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,880
It's a win-win.

56
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,280
That's interesting.

57
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,879
But the problem is, you can't rely solely on LARP games...

58
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:49,959
to sell your rooms.

59
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,399
Of course not.

60
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,160
I don't have the money for a major remodel,

61
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,559
but the hotel's excellent blackout and soundproofing...

62
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:57,999
already provide a great foundation.

63
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,079
So I'll just optimize...

64
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,560
the guests' sleep experience.

65
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:01,760
I'll upgrade the bedding.

66
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,919
Plus, most of our guests are flight crews...

67
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,959
who have been working all day.

68
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,720
So I'll also provide footbath buckets...

69
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,080
and herbal soak packs.

70
00:05:08,081 --> 00:05:10,200
Even though the rooms aren't luxurious,

71
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,120
I'll make sure the guests sleep soundly.

72
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:13,960
Okay.

73
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,840
That sounds much more interesting.

74
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,720
But why did you bring me to Hengshi?

75
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,280
To negotiate a collaboration.

76
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,400
I have all those rooms ready to be filled.

77
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:23,999
Besides,

78
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,360
what if he likes my idea...

79
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,560
and decides to invest?

80
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,960
All right.

81
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,080
Let's go.

82
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,839
Let's go give Fu Ming Yu...

83
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:36,840
a little shock.

84
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,439
Shock him with what?

85
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,759
Aren't you going to work with us at Bo'ao?

86
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:40,960
Why do you want to shock him?

87
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,600
Experience tells me...

88
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:43,840
not to put...

89
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,120
all my eggs in the same basket.

90
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,600
Grab my bag.

91
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,240
Wait.

92
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,960
Fu Ming Yu is so shrewd and stingy!

93
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,200
He...

94
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,400
Hurry up.

95
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:58,240
There's no way he'll invest in you.

96
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:00,800
I'll invest.

97
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:02,520
Brother-in-law, you're so wise.

98
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:05,160
Regarding the hotel rooms you mentioned,

99
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,760
I'll give you the contact info for the person in charge.

100
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,920
Also, I'll invest in my own name.

101
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,960
The amount might not be huge,

102
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,560
but it'll be enough for you.

103
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,880
Oh my gosh.

104
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,599
Brother-in-law, you've really impressed me today.

105
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:20,439
How can you have such a great investor's vision?

106
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,440
Wait.

107
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,639
You two are having a grand time calling each other in-laws.

108
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,280
Did you ask Ruan Si Xian if she agrees?

109
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,480
Your proposal impressed me today as well.

110
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,080
I thought you only did photography.

111
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:32,016
I didn't expect your hotel management concepts...

112
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,040
to be so advanced.

113
00:06:33,041 --> 00:06:34,760
I knew you had good taste, brother-in-law.

114
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,519
The two of you are making me feel sick.

115
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,480
I simply can't listen to this anymore.

116
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,720
- You're still here? - You're still here?

117
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:45,536
If you're uncomfortable, the exit is over there.

118
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,560
Suit yourself.

119
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,080
Trying to get rid of me, Fu Ming Yu?

120
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:53,800
I'm telling you, that's not happening.

121
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,480
Come on.
Don't just talk big.

122
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,480
Be specific. How much are you investing?

123
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,720
Not much.

124
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,160
Two million yuan.

125
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,400
Two million yuan?

126
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,480
- Is that not enough? - It's enough, really.

127
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:08,720
My startup capital is actually less than two million.

128
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,800
- Five million. - What's with the grand gesture?

129
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:14,599
Five million!

130
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,600
Don't shout.

131
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,440
No way.

132
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,720
I can't let your investment exceed mine by that much.

133
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,096
I'll invest two million as well.

134
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,120
All right?

135
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,480
We'll see.

136
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,480
Brother-in-law, today's talk was very pleasant.

137
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,840
Once the contract is signed,

138
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,920
our project will be officially launched.

139
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,600
Rest assured. No problem.

140
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,199
Brother-in-law, the two of us will head out now.

141
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,200
We won't bother you.

142
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,719
Brother-in-law, you're the best!

143
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,976
You're so wise, brother-in-law! We'll always support you!

144
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,039
- I... I can invest too! - Let's go.

145
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,079
- Fu Ming Yu, don't... - You...

146
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,159
Don't think you're the only one with money!

147
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,160
- I can invest too! - Let's go!

148
00:07:42,161 --> 00:07:43,439
- Why do you keep hitting me? - Bye!

149
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:44,440
I can invest money too!

150
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,480
Being called "brother-in-law" sounds so nice.

151
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,936
Zheng You An, what's that supposed to mean?

152
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,959
Do you really think Fu Ming Yu invested in you...

153
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,119
because of your proposal?

154
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:55,479
Let me tell you, he only invested in you...

155
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,480
because you kept calling him "brother-in-law".

156
00:07:56,481 --> 00:07:58,039
He lost himself in that title. That's why he invested.

157
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,240
That's quite insulting.

158
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,440
But it's okay.

159
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,600
As long as I get the funding, I don't care.

160
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,800
No,

161
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,239
what I mean is,

162
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:11,320
our relationship is much closer than yours with him.

163
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,759
I call him "brother-in-law",

164
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,120
so at least legally, we are related.

165
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:17,080
But what about us? What's our relationship?

166
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,079
Does it even need to be said?

167
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,080
Friends.

168
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,279
Partners at best,

169
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,640
though I'm still considering that.

170
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,319
Regarding our relationship, didn't you say before...

171
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,320
Do you regret it?

172
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:34,439
You unilaterally ended our relationship...

173
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,560
just because you thought it wouldn't end well, right?

174
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,960
What I'm saying is, I'm a better choice than Fu Ming Yu.

175
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,760
We have such great chemistry.

176
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,520
There's no need to look elsewhere.

177
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,600
You know what?

178
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,399
When I first found out that Fu Ming Yu liked Ruan Si Xian,

179
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,240
I thought they were the least likely couple.

180
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,496
The wealth gap and the difference in social status...

181
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:56,320
were enough to doom the relationship.

182
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,160
But look at them now.

183
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,960
They went for it without hesitation.

184
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,440
Now they look like a perfect match.

185
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:04,719
Why are we talking about them?

186
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:07,160
Fine, let's not talk about them. Let's talk about you and me.

187
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:08,320
My family...

188
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,600
hasn't been doing great lately,

189
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:13,120
but even so, we're still a good match, right?

190
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,480
But you...

191
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,119
Before we even truly moved to the next stage,

192
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:19,200
you gave our relationship a deferred death sentence.

193
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,120
All relationships...

194
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,360
go through ups and downs.

195
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,479
But when others face problems,

196
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,280
they think about how to solve them.

197
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:28,560
As for you,

198
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,536
you just solved the problem by cutting me out.

199
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:33,119
We hadn't even truly faced a single real problem.

200
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,440
It was all just your imagination.

201
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,880
And then you stand here wallowing in self-pity.

202
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,080
But whether it's the hotel...

203
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,600
or our relationship,

204
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,040
you've never truly trusted me.

205
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,080
Let's go. Why are you just standing there?

206
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,679
It's called making amends. Better late than never.

207
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,680
Do you understand?

208
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,760
I get it.

209
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,480
Well...

210
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,936
- Let me carry your bag. - It's part of my outfit.

211
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,216
Then I'll hold the door for you.

212
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,599
Don't touch it. It's automatic.

213
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,799
Then let me treat you to dinner. What do you want to eat?

214
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,680
- Be quiet. - BBQ? Steak?

215
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,280
Does he usually cook for you?

216
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:34,080
I cook occasionally. Like making instant noodles.

217
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:37,480
You know the extent of my cooking skills.

218
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,600
And what do you mean?

219
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,720
This is my place.

220
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,080
Yes, your place.

221
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,296
You work for him during the day,

222
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,920
and he cooks for you at night.

223
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,480
Your working relationship is quite complicated.

224
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,720
Where is Xiao Zhen?

225
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,520
She just called. She has left the airport and is on her way.

226
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,000
How has she been lately?

227
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
She's fine.

228
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:04,720
Every day, it's just studying and exams.

229
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,720
It has been over two years now.

230
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,600
She should have moved on by now.

231
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,360
The reason I've been putting off this dinner...

232
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,416
is because I didn't want her to overthink.

233
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,520
How should I put it?

234
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:20,280
On the surface, she seems to have moved past it.

235
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,160
But I recently discovered...

236
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,000
that she's using her phone to chat with an AI.

237
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,359
- With an AI? - Think of it this way.

238
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,719
She found an AI boyfriend...

239
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,880
as a replacement for Lu Ming.

240
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,160
It's a purely virtual relationship.

241
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,480
I'll get the door.

242
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,240
Ruan Ruan...

243
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:49,840
Mr. Fu, it's you.

244
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:52,879
I'm sorry. My flight was delayed.

245
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,560
It's okay. Please come in. They're inside.

246
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:58,960
Look at her.

247
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,080
Why are you acting so suspicious?

248
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,480
It was so startling.

249
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:08,120
When I opened the door and saw Mr. Fu in an apron,

250
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:09,720
I felt like I was back at work.

251
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:11,800
From now on,

252
00:12:11,801 --> 00:12:14,480
just think of him as Xiao Fu, the nanny.

253
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:18,760
I can't do that.

254
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,399
Are you two just sitting here eating seeds?

255
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,440
Why don't you go and help?

256
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,559
We would only get in the way. Why bother?

257
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:27,000
What are you so nervous about?

258
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:30,080
He's the one meeting his girlfriend's best friends.

259
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,880
He should be the nervous one.

260
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,720
- Exactly. - Good point.

261
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,480
Have some seeds.

262
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,480
It's him!

263
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:43,080
- It's him! - I really like him.

264
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,680
Really?

265
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,120
They look alike.

266
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,320
Let's eat.

267
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,200
Otherwise, the meat will get tough.

268
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,960
Eat up. What are you guys doing?

269
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:53,960
Thank you, Mr. Fu.

270
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,520
Do you want to try something else?

271
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,480
No, it's fine.

272
00:14:04,481 --> 00:14:05,800
I like green onions.

273
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,599
Wait.

274
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,600
What's up with you guys?

275
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,360
Nothing. We're just eating.

276
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,919
Is it because I'm here...

277
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,240
that everyone feels a bit uneasy?

278
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:19,320
How could that be?

279
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,240
The atmosphere is great right now.

280
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,840
I'm going to dig in now. I'll feast on this.

281
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:25,080
You don't have to do that.

282
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,920
Just eat normally.

283
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,679
He's not Mr. Fu right now.

284
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,400
He's Fu Ming Yu, my boyfriend.

285
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,720
The two of you should be finding fault with him.

286
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,160
What are you saying?

287
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,840
Mr. Fu is so perfect.

288
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,160
How could he have any faults?

289
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,320
It's after hours now. You don't need to say such things.

290
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,216
Also, since we're off the clock, you don't have to call me Mr. Fu.

291
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,240
Okay, Fu...

292
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,120
Then what should I call you?

293
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:49,400
Nothing else...

294
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:50,680
seems quite right.

295
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,520
What would be appropriate?

296
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,240
I've got one.

297
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:00,160
How about "brother-in-law"?

298
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,640
Does that not sound good?

299
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,280
Is it not right?

300
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,440
Is it awkward to say?

301
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,720
Brother-in-law!

302
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:34,080
Brother-in-law!

303
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,799
Stop it! You're so annoying!

304
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,040
How could you say that?

305
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,160
- Brother-in-law... - Well...
Money is hard to earn, brother-in-law.

306
00:15:40,161 --> 00:15:42,039
It's understandable if Xiao Zhen feels shy.

307
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,239
They have an employer-employee relationship.

308
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,400
What's with you, Xuan?

309
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:46,279
Why were you also so flustered that you couldn't eat...

310
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:47,480
and stumbling over your words?

311
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,320
You have no idea.

312
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,399
I used to think your Fu Ming Yu...

313
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:53,440
had a face that screamed "abstinence".

314
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,039
But I only realized today...

315
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,680
that his face actually screams "silence".

316
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:59,159
There's no way I can sit at the same table...

317
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,280
and eat or chat with him.

318
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,280
This won't do. Isn't this wrong of us?

319
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,880
Mr. Fu worked so hard to prepare dinner for us,

320
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,480
and we just kicked him out.

321
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,160
What else could we do?

322
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:13,079
You wouldn't enjoy your meal with him here.

323
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:15,000
I have to prioritize one side.

324
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,440
Just wait.

325
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,520
I'll have to coax him tonight.

326
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,159
Coax him?

327
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,719
He's our "brother-in-law", after all.

328
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,839
Is he easy to coax?

329
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:26,840
Not at all.

330
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:30,000
Don't be fooled by his cold and silent act in public.

331
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,960
When it's just the two of us,

332
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:33,160
he's a total clinger.

333
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,120
A clinger?

334
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:38,039
Then it seems the gift I brought...

335
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,720
might actually be useful.

336
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,600
Why did you bring a gift?

337
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,840
You didn't tell me.

338
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:44,600
Just some social etiquette.

339
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,440
What gift?

340
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,480
Wait and see.

341
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:07,800
This...

342
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:09,599
This isn't just social etiquette.

343
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,799
This could start a whole love story.

344
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,800
That's why we should leave early.

345
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,576
We don't want to get in the way of the story.

346
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:16,600
Go try it on.

347
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:17,840
Go on, try it on.
- Check the size. - Try it on.

348
00:17:18,841 --> 00:17:20,041
- Try it on. - See if it fits.

349
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,320
You're good.

350
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:26,360
Standard procedure.

351
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:28,080
You didn't even tell me.

352
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:30,520
You're just a kid. You don't get it.

353
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,720
Anyway, today, I've done my good deed for the day.

354
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,680
This...

355
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:45,680
This isn't right.

356
00:17:45,681 --> 00:17:48,280
I think this look is a bit too...

357
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,200
Superficial.

358
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,600
Are you kidding me?

359
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:55,319
You're disrespecting sexiness and mocking modesty.

360
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,559
What do you even call this?

361
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,639
Whatever.

362
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,480
At least I'm showing some effort.

363
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,399
Is it because we're both here?

364
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,599
Are you embarrassed?

365
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,080
What's there to be embarrassed about?

366
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:05,600
Just wait.

367
00:18:05,601 --> 00:18:06,760
Coaxing him like this...

368
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:08,040
will be more than enough.

369
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,040
- More than enough. - More than enough.

370
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,800
Is "brother-in-law" angry?

371
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,080
Brother-in-law.

372
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:01,240
I... I want to interview you.

373
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,640
How did you come up with the title "brother-in-law"?

374
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Ruan Si Xian,

375
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,760
do you think it's funny?

376
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,000
It's not funny.

377
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:13,840
But it's very cute.

378
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,840
Be good, don't be mad.

379
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,200
Don't be mad.

380
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:25,920
Ruan Si Xian, I'm being angry very seriously.

381
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,240
Stop grinning at me.

382
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:29,480
Do you realize how serious the problem is today?

383
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,360
I know.

384
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,839
I shouldn't have made you come back to eat alone.

385
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:35,919
Exactly.

386
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,056
I only said that to be polite.

387
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:38,960
I said, "Do you want me to go upstairs to eat?"

388
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,759
At a time like this, you should try to lighten the mood.

389
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:42,559
You shouldn't have taken me literally and kicked me out.

390
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,560
I was wrong.

391
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:46,960
That's a good attitude.

392
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:58,440
Be good. Don't be mad, okay?

393
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,400
I was wrong.

394
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,600
What are you doing?

395
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:07,720
Don't be mad anymore.

396
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:11,800
I knew it.

397
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:14,200
We're just not suited for dating at all.

398
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,879
Ruan Si Xian, listen to what you're saying.

399
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:19,279
I've prepared so many things today. How are we not suited?

400
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,320
We're suited for marriage.

401
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,640
Is that so?

402
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Say it again.

403
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:32,840
Say it again.

404
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,480
I've been kicked out?

405
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:03,159
This brother-in-law...

406
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,160
can't be coaxed at all.

407
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:22,080
Morning, Captain Yue.

408
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,640
For today's flight,

409
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,479
the weather on the outbound leg shouldn't be a problem.

410
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,600
But on the return leg,

411
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:37,560
we might encounter some precipitation in Jiangcheng.

412
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,896
So when the time comes, remember to take more fuel.

413
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,239
If we run into weather issues,

414
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:43,400
we'll have to circle in the air for a while.

415
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:45,840
Do you understand?

416
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,200
Roger.

417
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,760
If there are no questions,

418
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,480
prepare to board in five minutes.

419
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,119
Come on, keep up. Hurry up.

420
00:21:56,120 --> 00:21:57,640
Push it quickly. I'm in a hurry later.

421
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:58,840
Be careful. Watch it.

422
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,199
Just put it in that corner over there.

423
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,536
That will do. Thanks for your hard work.

424
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:02,560
Okay.

425
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:03,760
Come on, hurry up!

426
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,160
Keep up!

427
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,239
(Jiangcheng, Cloudy)

428
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:13,120
(Light rain forecast to begin in five minutes.)

429
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:17,040
Go!

430
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,360
My lady, I'm coming! This is the last one.

431
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,799
Look at the sky.

432
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:24,280
It's about to pour.

433
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,759
If it rains, my project will be delayed by another day.

434
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:28,719
My money is just going down the drain every day.

435
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:29,720
And you're still playing games?

436
00:22:29,721 --> 00:22:30,839
Can't you focus on something serious?

437
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,639
My lady, it's just a small job.

438
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:34,000
Why do you have to do it yourself?

439
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:35,399
If there aren't enough people,

440
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,559
just hire a few more.

441
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,880
That would cost more!

442
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:40,000
I have to pinch every penny every single day.

443
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:41,240
I don't have that much money.

444
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,240
How much more could two extra people cost?

445
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:45,079
The hotel isn't even running yet,

446
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:46,400
and I've already spent so much.

447
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,439
There will be plenty of things to spend money on later.

448
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:51,400
See? I offered to invest more, but you refused.

449
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:52,840
You...

450
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:56,560
Just keep playing.

451
00:22:58,840 --> 00:22:59,840
I'm done.

452
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:01,240
Come on.

453
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,120
Let's work.

454
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:04,880
Pruning the branches.

455
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:21,479
Hey, hurry up and pack everything up.

456
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:22,480
It's going to rain soon.

457
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Tong Le!

458
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:34,360
Why did you come out?

459
00:23:34,361 --> 00:23:36,399
Stop working. It's pouring. Hurry, go inside.

460
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,400
I'm almost done!

461
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,559
That's enough.

462
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:41,560
- Go inside. - Soon!

463
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:43,960
You're soaked through.

464
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,800
Let's go.

465
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:54,920
Dry yourself off.

466
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:55,960
You'll catch a cold.

467
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:58,479
In my old job,

468
00:23:58,480 --> 00:24:00,560
I was at the mercy of the weather.

469
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,240
Now that I'm running a bar,

470
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,880
I'm still at the mercy of the weather.

471
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,320
But I think it's quite nice.

472
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:12,799
When it rains here,

473
00:24:12,800 --> 00:24:14,280
it's like we're on a deserted island.

474
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:16,440
It's just you and me.

475
00:24:16,920 --> 00:24:19,200
Plus, we have wine and music.

476
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,720
It's perfect.

477
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:23,920
If I don't make money, how can I pay your salary?

478
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:29,160
I don't need a salary.

479
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:30,520
Then what do you want?

480
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:35,920
Forget it.

481
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:37,520
Whatever you're thinking,

482
00:24:37,521 --> 00:24:38,959
either the Labor Law won't allow it...

483
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:39,960
or I...

484
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:41,640
won't allow it.

485
00:24:57,280 --> 00:24:59,240
Ms. Wang, is the soup ready?

486
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:01,960
Ma'am, don't do it. Allow me.

487
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:04,240
It's okay. I'll just bring it over.

488
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,440
Ma'am, what's wrong?

489
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:14,079
- It's nothing. - You've scalded yourself.

490
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:15,080
I did scald myself a bit.

491
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,840
I'll get you some burn ointment.

492
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:30,360
Captain Yue!

493
00:25:30,361 --> 00:25:31,959
(Hengshi 5123's Captain Yue Yang Is Suddenly Incapacitated)

494
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:32,960
Peng Fei,

495
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:34,360
quickly secure Captain Yue.

496
00:25:35,760 --> 00:25:37,080
Don't just sit there. Secure him!

497
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:44,320
Captain, I've made an announcement.

498
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:46,096
There are no medical staff in the cabin.

499
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:48,200
Can we still land in this weather?

500
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,920
Come in. Carry Instructor Yue out and settle him.

501
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:53,496
Your job is to calm the passengers. Leave the rest to me.

502
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:54,520
Roger.

503
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:12,240
Careful.

504
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:14,720
Let me do it.

505
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,160
Come on.

506
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:22,400
Peng Fei, take the left seat.

507
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:25,096
Don't be nervous. It's just like our usual training.

508
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,160
Read the checklist for me.

509
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:27,520
Okay.

510
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:32,400
- Ladies and gentlemen, I'm sorry. - Excuse me.

511
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:34,280
We have a passenger who is not feeling well.

512
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:35,320
Please don't panic.

513
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:37,080
Yue Yang.

514
00:26:37,120 --> 00:26:38,360
Can you hear me, Yue Yang?

515
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:42,040
Mayday, mayday, mayday!

516
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:45,359
Jiangcheng Approach, Hengshi 5123. Captain incapacitated.

517
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:46,959
Requesting weather and approach conditions.

518
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:47,960
Requesting radar vectors.

519
00:26:47,961 --> 00:26:49,161
Requesting medical assistance.

520
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:50,719
Hengshi 5123. Mayday received.

521
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:52,440
Runway 22 is currently in use.

522
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:53,759
Current Jiangcheng weather...

523
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:55,136
is 120 degrees at 15 meters per second,

524
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,239
gusting 8 meters per second.

525
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,760
Wind direction varying between 030 and 140.

526
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,760
Temperature 19°C. QNH is 1002.

527
00:27:00,840 --> 00:27:01,840
Moderate showers, wet runway.

528
00:27:01,841 --> 00:27:03,320
Runway condition code is 5-5-5.

529
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:05,279
I have aircraft in holding and on approach.

530
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:06,280
Confirm your intentions.

531
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:09,600
Stand by. Hengshi 5123.

532
00:27:10,320 --> 00:27:11,320
This weather...

533
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:13,279
is exactly like the weather...

534
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:14,320
during my captain exam.

535
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,720
The examiner back then was Instructor Yue.

536
00:27:20,600 --> 00:27:22,520
Look. Is there any flight information?

537
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:26,040
- It's raining so hard. - I've been checking. No info.

538
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:29,160
Maybe we shouldn't leave today.

539
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,120
The weather is terrifying today.

540
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:33,320
With all this thunder and rain,

541
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:35,600
the people on the plane must be scared to death.

542
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,439
(Hengshi Air Flight Operation Status Monitoring)

543
00:27:59,440 --> 00:28:01,000
(Mayday: SH5123, Captain Incapacitated)

544
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:05,399
(Bai Yang)

545
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:06,439
Hello, Mr. Fu.

546
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:07,760
SH5123 has sent a distress call.

547
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,279
We have already initiated the emergency response plan.

548
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:10,679
(SH5123, Captain Incapacitated)

549
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:11,680
(Landing in Jiangcheng)
(Captain: Yue Yang)

550
00:28:12,681 --> 00:28:14,281
(Co-pilots: Ruan Si Xian, Shan Peng Fei)

551
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:17,960
Si Xian, I've calculated it.

552
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:19,720
Left crosswind is 29 knots.

553
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:20,760
Tailwind is 7 knots.

554
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:22,680
Landing distance is 2,168 meters.

555
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:24,320
But...

556
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:25,480
But what?

557
00:28:25,481 --> 00:28:26,719
With the captain incapacitated, the manual requires...

558
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,840
using autopilot for landing.

559
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:30,056
The limit for that is 15 knots. We've exceeded it.

560
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,320
Look at the situation we're in.

561
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:33,720
For a manual landing, the maximum crosswind is 32 knots.

562
00:28:34,080 --> 00:28:36,320
We just calculated 29 knots. That meets the standard.

563
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:37,959
Besides, Captain Yue is still unconscious.

564
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:39,440
He needs immediate medical attention.

565
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:41,976
We've already made a mayday call. Let's land as soon as possible.

566
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,000
Copy that.

567
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,000
Hengshi 5123,

568
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:47,120
we've decided to continue the approach.

569
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:48,240
Hengshi 5123,

570
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,840
contact Approach on 125.55.

571
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:53,440
Contact Approach on 125.55. Hengshi 5123.

572
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:00,680
Mr. Fu,

573
00:29:00,840 --> 00:29:02,480
Captain Yue Yang's condition is critical.

574
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:05,920
The tower reports heavy rain with strong gusts.

575
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:07,480
They're landing on Runway 22,

576
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,320
but the crosswind is very strong.

577
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:25,640
(Still angry?)

578
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,400
What does "mayday" mean?

579
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,720
Is it related to the band Mayday?

580
00:29:43,040 --> 00:29:44,040
Mayday?

581
00:29:44,480 --> 00:29:45,480
Where did you see that?

582
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:47,120
The news.

583
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,439
(Heavy Rainstorm Hits Jiangcheng, Hengshi Flight Sends Mayday Signal)

584
00:29:53,440 --> 00:29:54,440
What's wrong?

585
00:30:03,120 --> 00:30:04,120
Mom!

586
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:05,760
Let me see the burn. How bad is it?

587
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:08,639
Let's go to the hospital right now. We can't let it get infected.

588
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,800
An An, be quiet for a second.

589
00:30:10,440 --> 00:30:12,720
Hengshi 5123 is currently on approach.

590
00:30:13,120 --> 00:30:14,319
We will continue to monitor the situation...

591
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,640
and provide you with updates.

592
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,680
Phone.

593
00:30:19,080 --> 00:30:21,120
- Mom, don't panic. - Where is my phone?

594
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,720
Where's my phone?

595
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,640
- I just had it in my hand. - What's wrong?

596
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:26,880
Thank you.

597
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:32,360
Hello. The number you have dialed is powered off.

598
00:30:39,240 --> 00:30:40,640
All vehicles, follow my command!

599
00:30:40,720 --> 00:30:41,720
Everyone, get ready!

600
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,600
Prepare for rescue once the plane stops.

601
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,479
Repeat! All vehicles, follow my command.

602
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:47,359
Mr. Fu, people from the Regional Administration...

603
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:48,439
will be here soon.

604
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:49,640
They're here for a briefing.

605
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:50,840
Are you going over?

606
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,120
Leave it to Mr. Hu.

607
00:30:52,121 --> 00:30:53,441
- I'm staying right here. - Okay.

608
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:01,079
I'll get out first. Wait for me in the car.

609
00:31:01,080 --> 00:31:02,080
Xiao Zhen.

610
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:03,840
Don't worry.

611
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,480
In my heart, Ruan Ruan is the most outstanding female captain.

612
00:31:11,320 --> 00:31:12,320
Careful.

613
00:31:12,840 --> 00:31:13,840
Careful.

614
00:31:19,760 --> 00:31:21,360
Why can't I see anything from here?

615
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:24,560
Yan An, I can't see anything from here.

616
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:25,840
How will we know...

617
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:27,520
if Ruan Ruan's plane has landed safely?

618
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:29,656
Ma'am, please don't worry. I'll go and ask for you right now.

619
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:30,719
Then I'll go with you.

620
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:31,799
No, Mom. Your foot might get infected.

621
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,216
- Just let him go. - That's right, ma'am.

622
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:35,096
Even if you go now, you won't be able to get to the apron.

623
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,199
I'll go and ask for you right away.

624
00:31:36,200 --> 00:31:37,736
If there's any news, I'll call you immediately.

625
00:31:37,760 --> 00:31:38,760
- Okay. - I'll head off then.

626
00:31:38,761 --> 00:31:39,961
- Sorry for the trouble. - Go.

627
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:42,959
Hengshi 5123. Cleared for ILS approach.

628
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:44,496
Runway 22. Report when established on localizer.

629
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:45,719
Cleared for Runway 22 approach.

630
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:47,160
Will report localizer. Hengshi 5123.

631
00:31:49,120 --> 00:31:50,159
G/S. LOC Blue armed.

632
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:51,960
CAT III Dual. AP 1 plus 2.

633
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:53,240
Check.

634
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,680
Rain seems lighter on final approach.

635
00:31:56,800 --> 00:31:57,800
Gear down.

636
00:32:02,360 --> 00:32:03,840
Crosswind is within limits for now.

637
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:05,880
But any stronger and it'll exceed them.

638
00:32:06,160 --> 00:32:07,200
Turn on the wipers for me.

639
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:14,200
Why did the rain suddenly get heavier?

640
00:32:16,720 --> 00:32:17,760
Visual reference in sight.

641
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:18,960
Autopilot disconnected.

642
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:26,880
Mr. Fu.

643
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:28,520
The wind direction has changed.

644
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:34,760
CAT I.

645
00:32:34,761 --> 00:32:35,960
- Landing. - Check.

646
00:32:36,720 --> 00:32:38,080
- One hundred above. - Check.

647
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:39,480
- Decision height. - Continue.

648
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,200
The wind is shifting significantly.

649
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:47,240
Si Xian, the crab angle is very large.

650
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:48,960
Watch the crosswind.

651
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:04,040
The more urgent it is, the steadier we must be.

652
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:05,399
For the passenger in critical condition,

653
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,440
we must race against time.

654
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:09,200
But the safety of the other 181 passengers...

655
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:11,200
is also our responsibility.

656
00:33:25,040 --> 00:33:26,440
Xiao Zhen, don't wander off.

657
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:32,520
You should also check if Ruan Ruan sent you a message.

658
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:45,840
100.

659
00:33:51,280 --> 00:33:52,280
Si Xian,

660
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:53,640
the wind is erratic now.

661
00:33:59,280 --> 00:34:00,280
50.

662
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:04,080
40.

663
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:06,240
30.

664
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:08,320
20.

665
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:20,280
Retard.

666
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:23,400
Spoilers. Reverse green. Decelerate.

667
00:34:23,560 --> 00:34:25,640
It touched down!

668
00:34:29,520 --> 00:34:30,520
Direction! Direction!

669
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:44,360
The nose is back to center.

670
00:34:46,680 --> 00:34:47,720
Hengshi 5123.

671
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:49,040
Exit at B4.

672
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:51,160
Speed is too high. Unable to exit.

673
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:52,400
Hengshi 5123.

674
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:55,440
What's the situation?

675
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:57,040
Mr. Yan, don't worry!

676
00:34:57,560 --> 00:34:59,560
The plane is back on the centerline.

677
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:01,280
The wind direction suddenly shifted.

678
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:02,760
The speed isn't dropping.

679
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:04,280
Ruan Si Xian is on that plane.

680
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:10,240
Tailwind.

681
00:35:10,241 --> 00:35:11,720
Si Xian, tailwind is increasing.

682
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:14,239
(Hengshi Flight 5123 Hit With Increasing Tailwind)

683
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:15,400
The plane isn't slowing down.

684
00:35:15,560 --> 00:35:17,480
If this continues, we'll overrun the runway!

685
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:19,240
Hengshi 5123. Exit at B3.

686
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,360
Don't worry.

687
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:40,840
We believe in her.

688
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,880
I know.

689
00:35:42,881 --> 00:35:44,840
Hengshi 5123, exit at B2.

690
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:46,680
70 knots.

691
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:51,960
Crosswind is decreasing.

692
00:35:52,080 --> 00:35:53,360
Direction is under control.

693
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:54,800
Reverse thrust is available.

694
00:35:54,801 --> 00:35:57,120
(Ruan Si Xian Applies Second Reverse Thrust)

695
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:03,959
It's at B2.

696
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:05,599
Why hasn't it exited the runway yet?

697
00:36:05,600 --> 00:36:06,720
It should have turned off...

698
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:08,520
to exit the runway at B4.

699
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:10,040
But the speed didn't drop.

700
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:13,440
- What's the situation? - It still hasn't slowed down.

701
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:17,160
Lu Ming,

702
00:36:17,920 --> 00:36:18,920
if you're there,

703
00:36:19,400 --> 00:36:20,520
if you can hear me,

704
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:24,240
Please make the plane stop.

705
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:26,200
Ruan Ruan has to be safe.

706
00:36:34,320 --> 00:36:35,400
Ruan Si Xian, stop.

707
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:45,680
Hengshi 5123. Exit at B1.

708
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:49,520
Stop.

709
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:55,840
Stop!

710
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:33,960
- Brakes set. - Pressure in the green.

711
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:35,960
That scared me to death.

712
00:37:36,080 --> 00:37:37,080
Oh, my gosh.

713
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,240
My legs have gone weak.

714
00:37:43,680 --> 00:37:45,840
It's safe!

715
00:37:47,040 --> 00:37:49,320
It's safe!

716
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:51,000
Great!

717
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:53,040
Great!

718
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:56,080
It's safe.
Did it stop?

719
00:37:58,040 --> 00:37:59,200
Xiao Zhen, it landed!

720
00:38:01,080 --> 00:38:03,680
It landed! Ruan Ruan landed!

721
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:07,960
Hello, An An.

722
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:09,439
The plane has stopped!

723
00:38:09,440 --> 00:38:10,839
- How is it? - It's safe!

724
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:11,960
How is it?

725
00:38:13,720 --> 00:38:14,720
Say that again.

726
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:16,240
The plane has stopped!

727
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:17,560
Don't worry!

728
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:18,920
It stopped.

729
00:38:19,160 --> 00:38:20,679
- The plane has stopped. - It stopped.

730
00:38:20,680 --> 00:38:21,680
It stopped.

731
00:38:23,720 --> 00:38:25,400
Thank goodness it stopped.

732
00:38:25,640 --> 00:38:26,760
- It's okay. - It stopped.

733
00:38:27,120 --> 00:38:28,120
Thank goodness.

734
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:29,640
This is great.

735
00:38:36,720 --> 00:38:38,000
- Hello? - Xuan.

736
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:41,160
It's fine. It landed.

737
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:43,000
Ruan Ruan landed.

738
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:44,480
Good.

739
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,800
I knew our Ruan Ruan...

740
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:49,280
was the best.

741
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:57,480
Hengshi 5123,

742
00:38:58,120 --> 00:38:59,640
can you exit at your current position?

743
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:01,760
Exiting at B1.

744
00:39:03,080 --> 00:39:04,080
Hengshi...

745
00:39:04,520 --> 00:39:05,520
5123.

746
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:24,240
All vehicles, move out!

747
00:39:24,440 --> 00:39:25,679
Go!

748
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:26,880
- Get in! - Okay.

749
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:28,840
Get in the vehicle! Hurry!

750
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:01,160
In position. Brake set.

751
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:02,720
Pressure in green. Engine off.

752
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:03,920
Shutting down.

753
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:07,480
Disarm the slides.

754
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:08,680
Copy that, Captain Ruan.

755
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:12,240
All flight attendants,

756
00:40:12,640 --> 00:40:13,760
disarm slides...

757
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:15,280
and cross-check.

758
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:19,080
L1 disarmed. Cross-check.

759
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:21,320
R1 disarmed. Cross-check.

760
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:22,440
Rescue team, hurry!

761
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:24,160
Casualties confirmed. Hurry!

762
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,200
Over here!

763
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:28,720
Don't worry.
Everything is arranged.

764
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:31,440
Good.

765
00:40:45,240 --> 00:40:46,280
Watch your step, everyone.

766
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,440
- Watch your step. - Careful.
It's slippery.

767
00:40:48,640 --> 00:40:50,400
- Watch your step. - Careful. Let's go.

768
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:51,480
Slow down.

769
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,360
- Be careful. Don't rush. - Hurry!

770
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:54,800
- Watch your step. - This way.

771
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:56,040
- Be careful. - Be careful.

772
00:40:56,400 --> 00:40:57,479
- Slowly. - Watch out, it's slippery.

773
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,959
- Don't rush. - Be careful not to trip.

774
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,520
Watch your step. It's slippery.

775
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:01,880
Watch your step, everyone.

776
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:03,719
- Watch your step. - Be careful. It's slippery.

777
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:04,720
Be careful not to fall.

778
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:05,960
Slowly.

779
00:41:06,160 --> 00:41:07,160
Okay, take it slow.

780
00:41:07,920 --> 00:41:09,240
Watch your step. This way.

781
00:41:09,560 --> 00:41:10,840
- Be careful. - Watch your step.

782
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:13,480
- Don't rush. - Landed safely.

783
00:41:13,560 --> 00:41:14,560
Watch your step.

784
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:15,760
Gently.

785
00:41:16,440 --> 00:41:17,720
- Let's go. - Hurry.

786
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:20,680
Come over here.

787
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:21,880
- Let's go. - Let's go.

788
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:35,880
Don't move yet.

789
00:42:38,160 --> 00:42:39,600
Let me hold you for a little longer.

790
00:42:42,280 --> 00:42:43,280
Just now,

791
00:42:43,840 --> 00:42:45,320
were you all worried sick?

792
00:42:50,240 --> 00:42:51,280
But you did it.

793
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:54,040
And you did a great job.

794
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:56,920
You know what?

795
00:42:57,440 --> 00:42:58,640
For a moment there,

796
00:43:00,040 --> 00:43:01,080
I was really a bit scared.

797
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:07,200
What were you afraid of?

798
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:09,680
Boss, just give me a raise.

799
00:43:11,160 --> 00:43:12,240
I'm already all yours,

800
00:43:13,120 --> 00:43:14,720
and you're still thinking about a raise?

801
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,600
Even brothers keep clear accounts.

802
00:43:17,120 --> 00:43:18,400
So are you giving me one or not?

803
00:43:21,920 --> 00:43:22,920
Close your eyes.

804
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:52,920
(Departing Ep. 20 for Ep. 21)
